{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310866,"nonce":"lIsc0j90DAe+Oirrp2Z11yyKj9c=","title":"Shape-class bucket pool infrastructure (commit 7222541) — opt-in via RAYZOR_POOL=1, default disabled. POISON mode for catching UAF. ...","message":"Shape-class bucket pool infrastructure landed at commit 7222541. **Opt-in via `RAYZOR_POOL=1`**; default behaviour is unchanged from pre-pool baseline. Performance claim of \"removes alloc churn from the hot loop\" is **deferred** until the data-flow gap is closed (see [[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]]).\n\n**Why landed dormant:** under `RAYZOR_POOL=1 RAYZOR_POOL_STATS=1`, a 24-token llama-chat run reports `hits=0 misses=3029 pushes=0`. The pool is correctly plumbed end-to-end but transient activation tensors aren't reaching `rayzor_tensor_free` during inference. Two roots: (a) KV-cache reference holding suppresses Drop on activation tensors; (b) drop-analysis / `InsertFreePass` gap on transient ops (`binop_with_out`, `unary_with_out`, `bmm`, `matmul`, `matmul_t`, `scale` outputs). Shipping plumbing as a prerequisite chassis; activating it requires closing those data-flow gaps.\n\n**How to apply:** when proposing optimisations that assume `owns_data=true` implies canonical contiguity, this commit makes that true runtime-wide via the rewritten `rayzor_tensor_clone`. When proposing in-place fast-paths gated on `owns_data`, you can now trust the contiguity invariant. When designing kernels for view inputs (`!owns_data`), still check strides explicitly — only the owning side is canonical.\n\n\n**Pool**: `parking_lot::Mutex\u003cHashMap\u003cPoolKey, Vec\u003cPooledEntry\u003e\u003e\u003e` with FIFO eviction at two levels (per-bucket `RAYZOR_POOL_MAX_PER_BUCKET`=8, global `RAYZOR_POOL_MAX_TOTAL_MB`=256). Eviction invokes the caller-supplied `FreeFn` *after* releasing the bucket Mutex so the freer can safely call `malloc`/`free` without re-entering the pool. `PoolStats` Atomic* fields readable without lock for low-overhead diagnostics. `PooledEntry` Send+Sync; ownership transfers atomically between push/try_pop.\n\n**PoolKey three-way namespace isolation**:\n- Plain tensor: `(dtype, shape_hash)`\n- QTensor: `(0x80 | scheme, shape_hash)` — `0x80` bit prevents collision with plain dtypes\n- QTensor `group_size` folded into both `shape_hash` and synthetic `[rows, cols, group_size]` shape vec used for the bucket-walk collision check\n\nBucket-walk `entry.shape == requested` comparison is authoritative; hash collisions are safe.\n\n**Contiguity invariant** (the safety story): `rayzor_tensor_clone` now ALWAYS compacts to canonical row-major contiguous. Fresh data buffer of exactly `numel * dtype_size`, fresh shape + canonical strides arrays (NOT inherited from src), `owns_data=true`. `owns_data == true` runtime-wide implies canonical row-major strides AND `data_bytes == numel * dtype_size`. Pool admission cannot pick up a non-contiguous wrapper. See [[bugs-clone-view-passthrough-invariant]] (now FIXED).\n\n**Defence in depth**:\n- View producers (`permute`, `slice`, `transpose*`, `reshape`-aliased) set `owns_data=false` at construction\n- `rayzor_tensor_free` push gate requires `owns_data=true` — single chokepoint\n- `alloc_tensor`'s pool-hit path rewrites strides defensively (negligible cost), with `debug_assert!` that the parked strides matched canonical\n\n**Q4_K_M / Q6_K bypass**: `rayzor_qtensor_free` early-returns to direct `libc` free path when `scheme != QSCHEME_INT8` because `alloc_qtensor`'s `try_pop_qtensor` only revives INT8. Without this, Q4_K_M owning wrappers from `rayzor_qtensor_wrap_q4_k_m(take_ownership=1)` accumulated as a never-popped bucket leak.\n\n**Concurrency** (correct):\n- `push_inner_locked` holds the bucket Mutex across the `current_bytes` load + `max_total_bytes` comparison + park decision; two concurrent pushers cannot both observe under-budget and breach the cap\n- 8 threads × 1000 cycle stress test verifies exact `push == free` count after drain\n\n\n| Flag | Default | Effect |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| `RAYZOR_POOL` | unset | Pool disabled. Must be `=1` to enable. |\n| `RAYZOR_POOL_DISABLE` | unset | Force-disable; overrides `RAYZOR_POOL=1`. |\n| `RAYZOR_POOL_MAX_PER_BUCKET` | 8 | FIFO eviction threshold per bucket. |\n| `RAYZOR_POOL_MAX_TOTAL_MB` | 256 | Global byte cap (hard via Mutex-protected check). |\n| `RAYZOR_POOL_STATS` | unset | Atexit dump of hits / misses / pushes / evictions / hit_rate. |\n| `RAYZOR_TENSOR_POOL_POISON` | unset | Stamp `0xCD` on data buffer (and INT8 meta) at park + pop. Catches UAF from compiler drop-analysis regressions as obvious sentinel values; otherwise pool masks UAF as silent value corruption. |\n\n\n- Pool unit + stress: 16/16 in tensor_pool module\n- Clone contiguity: `tensor_clone_of_permuted_view_compacts_to_contiguous`, `tensor_clone_of_contiguous_is_independent`\n- QTensor scheme isolation: `q4_k_m_free_bypasses_pool`\n- Total runtime suite: 110/110 (pre-existing test-ordering SIGSEGV under `--test-threads=1` not introduced by this work)\n- llama-chat compare.sh: MATCH byte-for-byte vs llama.cpp\n- 128/128 haxe regression\n- Default-off bench within noise of pre-pool baseline\n\n\n1. **[[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]]** — most important. Transient activation tensors don't flow through `rayzor_tensor_free` during inference (KV-cache references + drop-analysis gap). Without closing this, the pool is dead infrastructure. Highest single-call-site test: a 24-token llama-chat under `RAYZOR_POOL=1 RAYZOR_POOL_STATS=1` should show pool hits and pushes \u003e 0.\n\n2. **`rayzor_tensor_clone` still bypasses `alloc_tensor`** — calls `libc::malloc` directly four times. If a future workload routes through clone heavily, pool benefit is bypassed there too. Extract the 4-malloc sequence in `alloc_tensor`'s miss path into an inner helper.\n\n3. **TAST aliased-move gap** — `var b = a; consume(a); b.ndim()` is not caught by current strict-`@:move` analysis (only the linear `var b = a; consume(a)` use-after-move case fires). Without the pool this surfaces as a SIGSEGV (loud); with the pool the freed buffer stays parked and the next alloc silently mutates `b`'s view. Close the TAST gap before flipping default-on. POISON mode partially mitigates by surfacing `0xCD` instead of stale data.\n\n4. **`rayzor_tensor_pool_reset` lifecycle hook** — exposed but never called from a process lifecycle. Long-running processes can hoard up to 256 MB indefinitely (capped at `RAYZOR_POOL_MAX_TOTAL_MB`). Wire a per-generation-step or per-test drain trigger if needed.\n\n5. **8 pre-existing `clippy::needless_range_loop` warnings in quant.rs** (lines 451, 660, 768, 1404, 1412, 1642, 1651, 1659) — not introduced by this work; predate the pool. Will flip CI green→red if `clippy -D warnings` is added as a gate.\n\n\n- [[project-move-clone-enforced]] — strict `@:move` makes the pool admission gate (`owns_data=true`) load-bearing; user cannot revive a moved binding because the source-level use is statically unreachable\n- [[project-addinto-fused-kernel]] — `addInto` removes per-step new-tensor alloc churn; pool would remove per-step shape-class alloc churn (KV-cache growth, attention scratch) once data flow is fixed\n- Future: SDOT/SMMLA quantised matmul (~3-5× on the ~80% of CPU that qmatmul takes) — pool composes cleanly; doesn't depend on the data-flow gap being closed\n\n\n- `wea2xoz42` — initial pool workflow (9 agents). Returned yellow with 6 must-fix items: latent clone-of-view footgun, push budget race, pool hit_rate=0%, Q4_K_M leak, POISON missing, clone bypasses alloc.\n- `wvy1r32el` — remediation (7 agents). Fixed clone contiguity, budget race, POISON, Q4_K_M gate, opt-in `RAYZOR_POOL=1` gate. All landed.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_tensor_pool` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}